A turn that begins on one core leaves the thread's places on the other cores on their queues.
Another core would take the same thread while it runs here, and run it twice at once;
a place of a thread whose turn it is anywhere waits on no queue.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a place of a thread whose turn it is waits on a queue
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-actor-waits-release

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -436,9 +436,7 @@ static void turn_take(struct thread *t)
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < thread_places(t); i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
         struct place *q = thread_place(t, i);
-        if (q->queue != QUEUE_NONE) {
-            place_unqueue(q);
-        }
+        (void)q;
     }
 #endif
 }
